            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary artery disease in diabetic patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1561-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is possible to decrease the rate of progression of coronary artery disease in diabetic patients by controlling all risk factors including hyperglycemia and by the prescription of statin and aspirin in high risk patients. After a coronary event, the management of the patient must be as optimal as possible in terms of pharmacological treatment and revascularization. &quot;Ever more&quot; is the key line in these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
